    "result_text": "All tests pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`). Here's what I implemented for the `customerCode` feature.\n\n## Summary\n\n`customerCode` (`<LAST3>-<NNNN>`) is now assigned during `POST /api/owners` and returned on reads. The logic is split by responsibility rather than piled into one class:\n\n1. **`CustomerCode`** (new helper, mirrors the existing `E164Telephone` style) \u2014 the *single definition of the format*: pure `format(lastName, sequence)` that upper-cases the first three letters (fewer if the name is shorter) and zero-pads the sequence to 4 digits \u2192 `\"SMI-0007\"`.\n\n2. **`AssignOwnerCustomerCode`** (new pipeline step) \u2014 *orchestration only*: derives the sequence as `ownerRepository.findAll().size() + 1` and sets the code on the built owner. It runs **before** `SaveOwner`, so the new owner isn't yet counted \u2192 the sequence is \"one more than the current number of owners.\" Wired into `owners.POST.yml` between `defaultRegistrationDate` and `save`, following the existing `Default\u2026` mutate-then-save pattern.\n\n3. **`Owner` entity** \u2014 added a persisted `customerCode` field/column (so it survives to the `GET` read-back), plus the matching `customer_code` column in all four schema dialects (hsqldb \u2014 used by tests \u2014 h2, postgres, mysql).\n\n4. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added `customerCode` as a `readOnly` property on the `Owner` response schema, alongside `displayName`/`initials`. MapStruct auto-maps it by name (no mapper change needed).\n\nThe acceptance test's `coreFormatAndGlobalSequence` passes: `smithers`\u2192`SMI-\u2026`, `jones`\u2192`JON-\u2026`, with the two suffixes differing by exactly 1.\n\nReuse notes: no new repository method was added \u2014 the existing `findAll()` supplies the count, keeping the interface and its three implementations untouched.",
